[FINAL-TEXT] I now have complete evidence. The picture is fully clear.

**sshswitch has:**
- Zero OSPF neighbors (empty neighbor table)
- Only directly-connected routes — no OSPF-learned routes, no default route
- bond0 **admin DOWN** (no `LOWER_UP` flag) despite both physical slaves (eth6/eth7) being up

**Chain of failure:**
`bond0 DOWN` → br_v1 can only use eth0 (toward switch4, wrong direction) → OSPF Hellos from sshswitch never reach router17 → no adjacency → sshswitch never learns any routes → Campus 2 traffic hits sshswitch with no route to forward → dropped.

